    "excerpts": [
      {
        "text": "\"We should start back,\" Gared urged as the woods began to grow dark around them.",
        "comment": "first sentence"
      },
      {
        "text": "Bran thought about it. “Can a man still be brave if he’s afraid?” “That is the only time a man can be brave,” his father told him.",
        "comment": "Chapter: Bran I"
      },
      {
        "text": "\"Yet our way is the older way. The blood of the First Men still flows in the veins of the Starks, and we hold to the belief that the man who passes the sentence should swing the sword. If you would take a man’s life, you owe it to him to look into his eyes and hear his final words. And if you cannot bear to do that, then perhaps the man does not deserve to die.\"",
        "comment": "Chapter: Bran I"
      },
      {
        "text": "Every noble house had its words. Family mottoes, touchstones, prayers of sorts, they boasted of honor and glory, promised loyalty and truth, swore faith and courage. All but the Starks. Winter is coming, said the Stark words.",
        "comment": "Chapter: Catelyn I"
      },
      {
        "text": "Some old wounds never truly heal, and bleed again at the slightest word.",
        "comment": "Chapter: Eddard I"
      },
      {
        "text": "\"Never forget what you are, for surely the world will not. Make it your strength. Then it can never be your weakness. Armor yourself in it, and it will never be used to hurt you.\"",
        "comment": "Chapter: Jon I"
      },
      {
        "text": "\"My mind is my weapon. My brother has his sword, King Robert has his warhammer, and I have my mind … and a mind needs books as a sword needs a whetstone, if it is to keep its edge.\"",
        "comment": "Chapter: Tyrion II"
      },
      {
        "text": "\"Let me tell you something about wolves, child. When the snows fall and the white winds blow, the lone wolf dies, but the pack survives. Summer is the time for squabbles. In winter, we must protect one another, keep each other warm, share our strengths. So if you must hate, Arya, hate those who would truly do us harm. Septa Mordane is a good woman, and Sansa … Sansa is your sister. You may be as different as the sun and the moon, but the same blood flows through both your hearts. You need her, as she needs you … and I need both of you, gods help me.\"",
        "comment": "Chapter: Arya II"
      },
      {
        "text": "\"The common people pray for rain, healthy children, and a summer that never ends,\" Ser Jorah told her. \"It is no matter to them if the high lords play their game of thrones, so long as they are left in peace.\" He gave a shrug. \"They never are.\"",
        "comment": "Chapter: Daenerys III"
      },
      {
        "text": "\"When you play the game of thrones, you win or you die. There is no middle ground.\"",
        "comment": "Chapter: Eddard XII"
      },
      {
        "text": "\"Night gathers, and now my watch begins. It shall not end until my death. I shall take no wife, hold no lands, father no children. I shall wear no crowns and win no glory. I shall live and die at my post. I am the sword in the darkness. I am the watcher on the walls. I am the fire that burns against the cold, the light that brings the dawn, the horn that wakes the sleepers, the shield that guards the realms of men. I pledge my life and honor to the Night’s Watch, for this night and all the nights to come.\"",
        "comment": "Chapter: Jon VI"
      },
      {
        "text": "\"The things we love destroy us every time, lad. Remember that.\"",
        "comment": "Chapter: Jon VII"
      }
    ],
